From b6b349a1e12ead10fa2df7952fa9160540b42979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO=1: an evicted graphics pipeline keeps
 its storage buffer pointer slots when it is translated again
 (zortos293/Lichii #1143); off by default

Ported from zortos293/Lichii PR #1143 (merged as d2eaae4, GPL-3.0-or-later), "vulkan: keep an
evicted graphics pipeline's storage buffer pointers when it is translated again".

Ours carries the eviction it fixes: PipelineCache::EvictUnusedPipelines (every 600 frames,
pipelines unused for 9000 frames). An evicted pipeline is translated again on its next use
(CreateGraphicsPipeline() from fresh GraphicsEnvironments), and GenericEnvironment::
IsCbufStorageBufferPointer classifies each constant buffer pointer slot by what it holds at that
moment. A slot that is null, unmapped or outside the GPU range then (around an area load) is
not a pointer in the new translation, so that pipeline reads zeros through it for the rest of
the session. Upstream: Ocarina of Time corruption that builds up over a long session and clears
on restart. Our compute rebuilds already seed their earlier slots (SeedStoragePointers); graphics
pipelines had nothing like it.

EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exactly "1"):
- every graphics pipeline records, per program, the slots its translation took as pointers
  (pointer-table entries included): from the FileEnvironments for pipelines built at boot, from
  the live environments for run-time ones (translated or made from a kept translation);
- EvictUnusedPipelines keeps those slots by key hash (VideoCommon::EvictedPointerSlots, at most
  8192 entries, an entry is dropped once taken);
- the next CreateGraphicsPipeline() of that key seeds them into the environments before the
  EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP check and the translation, so a re-translation never binds fewer pointers
  than the pipeline it replaces;
- a kept slot that would otherwise have been no pointer logs a Warning (first 32, then every
  1000th): "Graphics pipeline <hash> translated again after eviction: s<N>:c<I>[<off>] holds
  <value> (<reason>), kept as the storage buffer pointer it was (<n> so far)". That line is the
  field evidence: it shows the bug was hit in a run.
Off (unset): nothing is recorded, kept or seeded; translation and eviction as before. Layout
only: one pointer per GraphicsPipeline and an empty map in PipelineCache.

Out of memory: recording, keeping and seeding the slots are wrapped like the tree's other
bad_alloc survival code (SurviveBadAlloc; EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS=1 still ends the session). A
pipeline then goes without its slots, as with the switch off, and is never dropped for it.

Differences from upstream: our SeedStoragePointers stands in for upstream's KeepStoragePointers
(emplace vs insert_or_assign: the environments are fresh, nothing was asked yet); slots are
stored behind a pointer and only when a pipeline has any. Upstream's unit test is left out
(needs its test fixture). Not covered, as upstream: disk records captured with a slot null.

Shader prep: the switch is in the TranslationSwitches list only because the check script wants
every switch name the backend reads. It changes no kept translation (those are made at boot from
disk records, which are never seeded), but set, it changes the stamp like any listed switch: the
first run with it prepares a store of its own and stutters more. For an A/B test, give that arm
one warm-up run first (the stores of both arms are kept after that), or start the control arm
from a fresh store too.

Field test: only sessions long enough to evict (10 minutes or more, leaving an area and coming
back); the scripted test queue logs no evictions.

Checks: git apply --check and git apply on copies of the T88 core files, and on T88 with build
series 0493 to 0503 applied in order before it (0494, 0499 and 0501 touch the same files). Not
compiled, not run.
