+// EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO=1 (exact "1"; zortos293/Lichii #1143): a graphics pipeline evicted
+// after 9000 unused frames is translated again on its next use, and that translation classifies
+// each constant buffer pointer slot by what it holds right then. A slot that is null or unmapped
+// at that moment (around an area load) loses its storage buffer, and the new pipeline reads
+// zeros through it until a restart: corruption that builds up over a long session. With the
+// switch every graphics pipeline records the slots it bound as pointers, eviction keeps them by
+// key hash, and the next translation of that key takes them as pointers whatever they hold.
+// Off: nothing recorded, nothing kept, translation as before.
+bool EvictKeepSsbo() {
+    static const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO");
+    return on;
+}
